In article <YZ5F2vm00WB7RL8VUE@andrew.cmu.edu> dh07+@andrew.cmu.edu (David Hairston) writes:
>new in nh3.0f3 is the weapon known as an athame. this stumped my panel
>of D&D experts (puts their credibility on the line). what is the history
>on the athame outside of the dungeon? inquiring minds want to know ...

	The _athame_ is the special dagger used in rituals of hermetic
magic.  It is not a sacrificial dagger, but rather a magical instrument
like a wand, candle, or incense.

	The word can also be used for a special dagger in other traditions,
but I'm less sure of what is and is not done with it.  For an interesting
idea about the athame (which may well have been the inspiration for using
it in NH3--ask one of the development team about that), try the book, _With
a Single Spell_, I believe by Lawrence Watt-Evans.  'Twas a really good
read, and the idea of an athame in it works quite well for Hack.

